  "/bridal-makeup-Bangalore": {
    sections: [
      { h: "Local Setting and the Way Families Celebrate", p: ["Family events in HSR Layout can move between homes, community spaces, banquet venues, hotels and other event locations. A bride may be coordinating relatives arriving from different parts of Bengaluru while also managing her own work, shopping, fittings, photography and wedding schedule. Convenience matters, but so does having enough time to prepare without feeling rushed. Makeup should be planned around the actual ready time and the movement between functions."] },
      { h: "Culture, Festivals and the Meaning Behind the Occasion", p: ["Bengaluru's wider festival calendar includes Ugadi, Deepavali, Ganesh celebrations, Navaratri and other religious and community occasions. Families may combine regional traditions with contemporary styling. For a bride, cultural requirements can affect the choice of saree or lehenga, jewellery, hair, bindi, eye definition and the overall level of makeup. The objective is not to impose a fixed traditional look, but to understand what the occasion means to the family and then build a coordinated appearance."] },
      { h: "How the Wedding Journey Changes from One Function to Another", p: ["An HSR Layout wedding may have several visual chapters: engagement, Haldi or Mehendi where applicable, wedding ceremony, family photographs, reception and post-wedding or pre-wedding photography. A bride may want a fresh and elegant engagement look, a more detailed bridal look for the ceremony, and a more glamorous evening appearance for the reception. The same approach can also be applied to intimate family celebrations and milestone parties."] },
      { h: "The Bride's Perspective: Confidence, Comfort and Feeling Like Herself", p: ["A bride often carries several expectations at once. She may want to look beautiful for her partner, feel comfortable around family, honour cultural traditions and still recognise herself in the mirror. She may have saved reference photographs but need help understanding what will actually suit her face, skin, outfit and jewellery. Rekha's consultation-led approach can turn those references into an individual plan instead of simply reproducing a trend."] },
      { h: "Occasion-to-Service Planning with Rekha Krishnamurthy", cardTable: [
        ["Engagement", "Engagement Makeup", "A polished, defined look that feels special without automatically becoming the full intensity of wedding makeup."],
        ["Wedding Ceremony", "Bridal Makeup", "A complete bridal look planned around ceremony timing, outfit, jewellery, skin preparation, longevity and photography."],
        ["Wedding Trial", "Trial Makeup", "A practical opportunity to discuss references, preferences, finish and the overall direction before the wedding day."],
        ["Skin Preparation", "Skin Consultation", "Helps identify preparation needs and allows the makeup plan to account for skin condition and desired finish."],
        ["Reception", "Party Makeup / Bridal Makeup", "A reception can have a separate evening direction, with more definition or glamour according to the outfit and venue."],
        ["Family Function", "Non-Bridal Makeup", "Polished makeup for mothers, sisters, relatives or guests who need event-ready grooming without bridal intensity."],
        ["Pre-Wedding Shoot", "Photoshoot Makeup", "Planned for changing outfits, backgrounds, lighting and camera requirements."],
        ["Creative Campaign", "Editorial Makeup", "For fashion-forward, concept-led or editorial photography where makeup is part of the visual story."],
        ["Fashion Event", "Fashion Makeup", "For runway, fashion content, designer shoots or styling-led projects requiring a deliberate visual direction."],
        ["Groom", "Groom Makeup", "Camera-ready grooming and complexion refinement for the groom when required."],
        ["Camera-Focused Finish", "HD Makeup", "Can be considered when a refined, photography-conscious finish is required."],
        ["Lightweight / Long-Wear Finish", "Airbrush Makeup", "Can be considered based on skin, finish preference, event conditions and photography needs."],
      ] },
      { h: "Building One Complete Wedding Beauty Plan", p: ["For a bride with several functions, the strongest approach is to plan the looks as a connected sequence rather than booking every service independently. The engagement can establish a polished but distinct appearance; the main wedding can receive the most detailed bridal planning; a reception can move toward a different evening expression; family functions can use Non-Bridal Makeup; the groom can receive Groom Makeup; and pre-wedding photography can be handled through Photoshoot Makeup. A Makeup Trial can be used when the bride wants to discuss and test the direction in advance, while Skin Consultation can help organise preparation. HD Makeup and Airbrush Makeup remain technique choices that should be matched to the bride's skin, desired finish, venue and photography rather than treated as automatic requirements."] },
      { h: "From the Ceremony to the Camera", p: ["Makeup needs to work in two places at once: in the room where the bride is getting ready and in the photographs that remain after the event. Complexion, texture, eye definition, lip colour and overall balance should therefore be considered with the actual lighting and photography style. An outdoor pre-wedding shoot, a traditional morning ceremony, an indoor reception and a fashion-led editorial are different environments. Matching the makeup service to that environment helps the bride avoid using one identical look for every occasion."] },
      { h: "Ready to Plan Your HSR Layout Wedding Makeup?", p: ["The purpose of consultation is to understand your preferences and translate them into a practical plan. The result should feel appropriate to the location and culture while remaining unmistakably yours."], ctas: [{ label: "Enquire About Bridal Makeup", to: "/contact?service=Bridal" }, { label: "Talk to Rekha", href: "whatsapp", secondary: true }] },
    ],
    faq: [
      ["What makeup services can a bride book with Rekha in HSR Layout?", "The service plan can include Bridal, Engagement, Non-Bridal, Party and Photoshoot Makeup, with HD or Airbrush techniques considered where appropriate. Trial and Skin Consultation can also support wedding preparation."],
      ["Can my engagement and wedding makeup be completely different?", "Yes. Each event has its own outfit, jewellery, lighting and emotional setting, so the makeup direction can be planned separately."],
      ["Can Rekha plan makeup for the groom and family members?", "Groom Makeup can support camera-ready grooming, while Non-Bridal Makeup can be considered for family members and guests."],
      ["Should I choose HD or Airbrush for my HSR Layout wedding?", "The choice should follow your skin, desired finish, venue, event duration and photography requirements rather than being selected only because of the technique name."],
      ["Can I discuss my preferred makeup style before booking?", "Yes. Sharing your references, event schedule, outfit, jewellery, skin concerns and the looks you do not want can make the consultation more useful."],
    ],
  },
